#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063947 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064360 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68cd4840-bb77-5065-884a-ce1c8c309cd0" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Fraction of Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "78675372-1e29-5088-8907-52d9e54124e1" :question/math-academy-id "e-13083" :question/problem "What is $\\dfrac {\\left(\\dfrac 1 4\\right)} {\\left(-\\dfrac 3 7\\right)}$ expressed as a single fraction?" :question/worked-solution "First, remember that a fraction represents a division.  So, a fraction of fractions is a division of two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(\\frac{1}{4})}{(-\\frac{3}{7})} & =\\frac{1}{4}÷(-\\frac{3}{7})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that dividing by $-\\dfrac{3}{7}$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal $-\\dfrac{7}{3}.$ We can use this fact to simplify the fraction above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}÷(-\\frac{3}{7}) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\times (-\\frac{7}{3}) & = \\\\ -\\frac{1\\times 7}{4\\times 3} & = \\\\ -\\frac{7}{12} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(\\frac{1}{4})}{(-\\frac{3}{7})} & =-\\frac{7}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the fact that a positive number times a negative number gives a negative number."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063948 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064361 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ca49b4e-a4fa-5a67-9334-12e8656b5d1a" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Counting Number by a Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "3bad12f4-14b2-5ab6-a1db-9d460b9a26ca" :question/math-academy-id "e-13084" :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac{\\left(-3\\right)} {\\left(-\\dfrac 3 5\\right)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, remember that a fraction represents a division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(-3)}{(-\\frac{3}{5})}=-3÷(-\\frac{3}{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $-3 =- \\dfrac{3}{1}$ and dividing by $-\\dfrac{3}{5}$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal $-\\dfrac{5}{3}.$ We can use these facts to simplify the fraction above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)÷(-\\frac{3}{5}) & = \\\\ (-\\frac{3}{1})÷(-\\frac{3}{5}) & = \\\\ (-\\frac{3}{1})\\times (-\\frac{5}{3}) & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\times 5}{1\\times 3} & = \\\\ \\frac{15}{3} & = \\\\ 5 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\left(-3\\right)} {\\left(-\\dfrac 3 5\\right)} = 5.\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the fact that a negative number times a negative number gives a positive number."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063949 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064362 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56936b9b-2b52-58a7-ae3f-7d51492b8247" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Fraction by a Counting Number"}] :question/id #uuid "87974d27-c494-5b1a-84e9-03e39f3e0b1c" :question/math-academy-id "e-13086" :question/problem "Calculate $\\dfrac{\\left(-\\dfrac 3 2\\right)}{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can use either of the following two methods.\n\n**Method 1 - The Long Way** \n\nFirst, remember that a fraction represents a division:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\left(-\\dfrac 3 2\\right)}{6} = \\left(-\\dfrac 3 2\\right)  \\div 6\n$$\n\nNow, recall that dividing by $6$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal $\\dfrac{1}{6}.$ We can use this fact to simplify the fraction above: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-\\frac{3}{2})÷6 & = \\\\ (-\\frac{3}{2})\\times (\\frac{1}{6}) & = \\\\ -\\frac{3\\times 1}{2\\times 6} & = \\\\ -\\frac{3}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n- \\dfrac{3}{12}  = - \\dfrac{3 \\div 3}{12 \\div 3}  = -\\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\left(-\\dfrac 3 2\\right)}{6}= -\\dfrac14\n$$\n\n \n\n**Method 2 - The Quick Way**\n\nThe result will have the same numerator as the top fraction, and the denominator is just the product of the two denominators: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{2})}{6} & = \\\\ \\frac{-3}{2\\times 6} & = \\\\ -\\frac{3}{12} & = \\\\ -\\frac{3÷3}{12÷3} & = \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4} & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064360 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68cd4840-bb77-5065-884a-ce1c8c309cd0" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Fraction of Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "219210f0-ae9d-5c25-bfa0-285a2895557a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "219210f0-ae9d-5c25-bfa0-285a2895557a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490573} :answer-field/id #uuid "df6c9788-4bdb-5360-8148-5d2109336609" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491092}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "11f803ec-fc39-5be9-aa77-adbf9149db85" :question/math-academy-id "q-185358" :question/problem "Expressed in its simplest form, $\\frac{\\,(-\\frac{5}{4})\\,}{(-\\frac{1}{8})}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, remember that a fraction represents a division.  So, a fraction of fractions is a division of two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\,(-\\frac{5}{4})\\,}{(-\\frac{1}{8})}=(-\\frac{5}{4})÷(-\\frac{1}{8})\n$$\n\nNow, recall that dividing by $-\\frac{1}{8}$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal $-\\frac{8}{1}.$ We can use this fact to simplify the fraction above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}(-\\frac{5}{4})÷(-\\frac{1}{8}) & = \\\\ (-\\frac{5}{4})\\times (-\\frac{8}{1}) & = \\\\ \\frac{5\\times 8}{4\\times 1} & = \\\\ \\frac{40}{4} & = \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\,(-\\frac{5}{4})\\,}{(-\\frac{1}{8})}=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064776 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064361 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ca49b4e-a4fa-5a67-9334-12e8656b5d1a" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Counting Number by a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf05019e-0fbb-5909-bdc7-441afa5579c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062714} {:answer/id #uuid "d4630dd5-db80-5a2c-8abb-69a118e71dfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062715} {:answer/id #uuid "e391f5b4-0444-5612-9d5d-cfb8b9723815" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062716} {:answer/id #uuid "556d0f48-496d-5b83-a01c-ed647970c8c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062717} {:answer/id #uuid "644225ae-897f-5530-9615-d488c54d900a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e391f5b4-0444-5612-9d5d-cfb8b9723815" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062716} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0296223-0afa-55c4-985e-ee00bd370614" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062713}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6c3cdbb7-2f20-5471-9a71-577081e6a156" :question/math-academy-id "q-43479" :question/problem "$\\frac{3}{(\\frac{7}{3})}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, remember that a fraction represents a division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{(\\frac{7}{3})}=3÷\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $3=\\frac{3}{1}$ and dividing by $\\frac{7}{3}$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal $\\frac{3}{7}.$ We can use these facts to simplify the fraction above:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3÷\\frac{7}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{1}\\times \\frac{3}{7} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\times 3}{1\\times 7} & = \\\\ \\frac{9}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{(\\frac{7}{3})}=\\frac{9}{7}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491190 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064360 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68cd4840-bb77-5065-884a-ce1c8c309cd0" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Fraction of Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b98cca8-6f0e-5482-9fa8-f7aeb424a305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490562} {:answer/id #uuid "69c8c086-db77-5758-967f-00696124f83f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490709} {:answer/id #uuid "7b71d305-a5a2-5d89-92a2-1dc57deb1bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490757} {:answer/id #uuid "a89968b9-3ad0-5516-ace6-ad93f1456e61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490849} {:answer/id #uuid "aab949d1-ff11-5cbe-a57e-c6e2603a0932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b71d305-a5a2-5d89-92a2-1dc57deb1bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490757} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3466160-186f-5215-84d6-837a7ed4ec4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491102}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2af5d91-5331-52df-9dc3-29a55153bfaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-43486" :question/problem "$\\frac{(\\frac{3}{7})}{(\\frac{1}{4})}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, remember that a fraction represents a division.  So, a fraction of fractions is a division of two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(\\frac{3}{7})}{(\\frac{1}{4})}=\\frac{3}{7}÷\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that dividing by $\\frac{1}{4}$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal $\\frac{4}{1}.$ We can use this fact to simplify the fraction above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7}÷\\frac{1}{4} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{7}\\times \\frac{4}{1} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\times 4}{7\\times 1} & = \\\\ \\frac{12}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{(\\frac{3}{7})}{(\\frac{1}{4})}=\\frac{12}{7}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491217 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064362 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56936b9b-2b52-58a7-ae3f-7d51492b8247" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Fraction by a Counting Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1750e457-61df-5f93-b615-35b2f02cf305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490557} {:answer/id #uuid "5b321ef0-fa18-53af-9de3-8bac3c88ce32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490682} {:answer/id #uuid "91f1e84e-b335-5652-bf66-1bfe42b9aa1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490806} {:answer/id #uuid "9922953e-e34d-59ba-a9f1-d4d61a61aa52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490826} {:answer/id #uuid "b09b4a98-9578-5f56-ac72-344906f876cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b09b4a98-9578-5f56-ac72-344906f876cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490863} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f53ff46-6bcb-5804-9c51-551d655fc687" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f784b6ba-5095-5d61-b18c-c45f932db76c" :question/math-academy-id "q-43489" :question/problem "$\\frac{(-\\frac{14}{3})}{(-8)}=$" :question/worked-solution "We can use either of the following two methods.\n\n**Method 1 - The Long Way**\n\nFirst, remember that a fraction represents a division:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(-\\frac{14}{3})}{(-8)}=(-\\frac{14}{3})÷(-8)\n$$\n\nNow, recall that dividing by $-8$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal $-\\frac{1}{8}.$ We can use this fact to simplify the fraction above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-\\frac{14}{3})÷(-8) & = \\\\ (-\\frac{14}{3})\\times (-\\frac{1}{8}) & = \\\\ \\frac{14\\times 1}{3\\times 8} & = \\\\ \\frac{14}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{14}{24}=\\frac{14÷2}{24÷2}=\\frac{7}{12}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{(-\\frac{14}{3})}{(-8)}=\\frac{7}{12}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - The Quick Way**\n\nThe result will have the same numerator as the top fraction, and the denominator is just the product of the two denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(-\\frac{14}{3})}{(-8)} & = \\\\ \\frac{-14}{3\\times (-8)} & = \\\\ \\frac{-14}{-24} & = \\\\ \\frac{-14÷2}{-24÷2} & = \\\\ \\frac{7}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064361 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ca49b4e-a4fa-5a67-9334-12e8656b5d1a" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Counting Number by a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d1ea965-b653-537d-891c-225d500492d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490532} {:answer/id #uuid "2b8cac6b-3adc-5b5a-be21-3757ca7d66de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490596} {:answer/id #uuid "32ba64b6-8f8c-5b2c-9521-0cad7a6d4ce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490608} {:answer/id #uuid "7f25c3b5-76c3-5920-bdf2-e88ae7188124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490764} {:answer/id #uuid "f21e0a43-a88c-5092-b67f-7a7fbd7a577f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f25c3b5-76c3-5920-bdf2-e88ae7188124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490764} :answer-field/id #uuid "abea8f89-7891-58cb-8e3f-b822bc185677" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0005d92-ca31-5bc9-800e-ea467608e665" :question/math-academy-id "q-99765" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\,\\,(-4)\\,\\,}{(\\frac{1}{5})}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, remember that a fraction represents a division:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\,\\,(-4)\\,\\,}{(\\frac{1}{5})}=(-4)÷\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $-4=-\\frac{4}{1}$ and dividing by $\\frac{1}{5}$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal $\\frac{5}{1}.$ We can use these facts to simplify the fraction above:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-4)÷\\frac{1}{5} & = \\\\ (-\\frac{4}{1})\\times \\frac{5}{1} & = \\\\ -\\frac{4\\times 5}{1\\times 1} & = \\\\ -\\frac{20}{1} & = \\\\ -20 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\,\\,(-4)\\,\\,}{(\\frac{1}{5})}=-20.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491189 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064362 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56936b9b-2b52-58a7-ae3f-7d51492b8247" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Fraction by a Counting Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32bca134-6367-5be4-9fd2-5d82101d533a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490609} {:answer/id #uuid "61eb38f1-6922-58af-8b15-1c45bf4f22a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490694} {:answer/id #uuid "834381da-ec1c-5b75-9720-f4882787a1ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490776} {:answer/id #uuid "9856080b-5615-58ba-9305-8f394edcbc9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490824} {:answer/id #uuid "d3c6ed7d-9644-5e4e-a9ee-748599da8dad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9856080b-5615-58ba-9305-8f394edcbc9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490824} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8815dfd-179a-5c5e-bb6e-8c58a712bc57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491096}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b0a96863-abdb-5fbd-be57-181eec5befbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-99769" :question/problem "$\\frac{(\\frac{7}{4})}{7}=$" :question/worked-solution "We can use either of the following two methods.\n\n**Method 1 - The Long Way**\n\nFirst, remember that a fraction represents a division:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(\\frac{7}{4})}{7}=\\frac{7}{4}÷7\n$$\n\nNow, recall that dividing by $7$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal $\\frac{1}{7}.$ We can use this fact to simplify the fraction above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{4}÷7 & = \\\\ \\frac{7}{4}\\times \\frac{1}{7} & = \\\\ \\frac{7\\times 1}{4\\times 7} & = \\\\ \\frac{7}{28}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{28}=\\frac{7÷7}{28÷7}=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{(\\frac{7}{4})}{7}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - The Quick Way**\n\nThe result will have the same numerator as the top fraction, and the denominator is just the product of the two denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(\\frac{7}{4})}{7} & = \\\\ \\frac{7}{4\\times 7} & = \\\\ \\frac{7}{28} & = \\\\ \\frac{7÷7}{28÷7} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064362 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56936b9b-2b52-58a7-ae3f-7d51492b8247" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Fraction by a Counting Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "101bedaa-1d23-5c71-acab-0e6d2fa138fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490542} {:answer/id #uuid "10694063-5723-5959-b976-e8be9c93ac53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490544} {:answer/id #uuid "2a46a3d3-5441-51d1-a705-2184fded9e3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490592} {:answer/id #uuid "2d5c6dcb-c785-52d6-847d-e13376bf3e3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490599} {:answer/id #uuid "f4264b47-3558-59ba-bc2d-0756e456b5b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4264b47-3558-59ba-bc2d-0756e456b5b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490978} :answer-field/id #uuid "41a56275-c6fa-56a6-b15e-4abe5e29fee8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e483ad67-316a-51cc-8531-219d3a80b4f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-99773" :question/problem "$\\frac{(-\\frac{7}{4})}{(-9)}=$" :question/worked-solution "We can use either of the following two methods.\n\n**Method 1 - The Long Way**\n\nFirst, remember that a fraction represents a division:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(-\\frac{7}{4})}{(-9)}=(-\\frac{7}{4})÷(-9)\n$$\n\nNow, recall that dividing by $-9$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal $-\\frac{1}{9}.$ We can use this fact to simplify the fraction above: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-\\frac{7}{4})÷(-9) & = \\\\ (-\\frac{7}{4})\\times (-\\frac{1}{9}) & = \\\\ \\frac{7\\times 1}{4\\times 9} & = \\\\ \\frac{7}{36}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{(-\\frac{7}{4})}{(-9)}=\\frac{7}{36}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - The Quick Way**\nThe result will have the same numerator as the top fraction, and the denominator is just the product of the two denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(-\\frac{7}{4})}{(-9)} & = \\\\ \\frac{-7}{4\\times (-9)} & = \\\\ \\frac{-7}{-36} & = \\\\ \\frac{7}{36} & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
